:: More Time Needed [event main_quest] {"position":"3150,125","size":"100,100"}
I find $sister.callName on her bed, half watching reels, half arguing with a comment section. The prototype is in my hoodie pocket. I drop onto the arm of her reading chair like I'm only passing through.

<<silently>>
<<set _msgs = [
  { who: $player,  text: "Hey, quick question. I'm a little short this week. Any chance you could spot me enough to cover the rest of the rent?" },
  { who: $sister,  text: "I wish, but I'm broke until Sunday. Do a round of chores and ask $mom.callName afterwards, that works every single time." },
  { who: $player,  text: "I would, but I'm buried today. If I spend two hours on dishes and vacuuming, I'm never going to make my deadline." },
  { who: $sister,  text: "Well, that's how it works around here. You make yourself useful and people are nice to you. Welcome home." },
  { text: "She says it as a joke, flicking to the next reel. It's also the most honest thing anybody in this house has said to me since I got back, and she has no idea she said it." },
  { text: "I wake the prototype with a thumb press. The hum is barely there, like an air conditioner you only notice once it stops. I keep my voice easy." },
]>>
<</silently>>
<<Chat _msgs>>
<<silently>>
<<UseQuestDevice $player>>
<<set _msgs = [
  { who: $player,  text: "I'm not trying to dodge anything, I swear, I really need the time. I finally had a breakthrough with the prototype, and if I stop now I'm going to lose the thread. And come on, we've always covered for each other when it mattered." },
  { who: $sister,  text: "We have, sure. That still doesn't magically put any money in my account." },
  { who: $player,  text: "Then how about this. Could you do the chores for me instead? Dishes, counters, recycling, a quick vacuum, so it all looks done when $mom.callName gets home. I'll leave a note with my name on it. She'll relax, maybe float me a little, and I get to keep my head above water." },
  { who: $sister,  text: "So I do the chores, and you take the credit." },
  { who: $player,  text: "I take some pressure off $mom.callName, and I get to finish what I'm working on. And you'd be doing it because you're a good person and you secretly like me. Please?" },
  { text: "I nudge the dial down a notch. Her shoulders loosen, and for the first time she's actually thinking about it instead of looking for a way out." },
]>>
<</silently>>
<<Chat _msgs>>
<<silently>>
<<DevicePulse "-1">>
<<set _msgs = [
  { who: $sister,  text: "You're so annoying when you're sincere, you know that? I'm going to be rolling my eyes about this for a week." },
  { who: $player,  text: "Roll them all you want. I'll owe you a big one." },
  { who: $sister,  text: "Fine, I'll do your chores. You write the note and sign it so $mom.callName sees it. If she gives you anything, great, and if she doesn't, you still owe me a proper thank-you and absolutely no gloating." },
  { who: $player,  text: "Thank you. That's the proper one. And no gloating, I promise." },
  { who: $sister,  text: "I honestly have no idea why I'm agreeing to this. Hand me the dish towel and get out of here before I come to my senses." }
]>>
<</silently>>
<<Chat _msgs>>

I stick the note on the fridge: Dishes ✔ Counters ✔ Recycling ✔ Vacuum ✔ ~$player.name.

Water starts running in the kitchen, and the vacuum growls awake a minute later. When she walks past with the recycling bag, she gives me a look that's half confused about why she said yes and half a warning not to make this a habit.

<<UpdateStat "+" "Corruption" 1>>
<<UpdateStat "+" "SisterCorruption" 1>>
<<silently>>
<<ProfileLog $sister "Taking Over the Chores" "With a little nudge from $company.prototype.name she agreed to do the house chores for me, so I have more time for the prototype.">>
<<NextQuest $player>>
<</silently>>
<<ReturnFromEvent>>
<<UseAction>>